  "$comment": "font.example.json: a complete, valid font.json for a fictional 'Example' family, to copy and edit. The schema is templates/font.schema.json and forbids unknown keys, so the key-by-key explanation lives in references/variable-font-build.md ('font.json, key by key'). Paths are relative to this file; with templates/concepts.example.js beside it, this file EXPORTS as it stands (node scripts/export.js --font templates/font.example.json --group roman OUT.json), and BUILDS with the reviewed requirements named: build.py needs a requirements.json beside font.json or --requirements (here --requirements templates/requirements.example.json, whose required characters this generator draws), or an explicit --no-requirements, which the manifest records. Reviewed expectations (floors, axes, characters, titles) are written separately in requirements.json: see templates/requirements.example.json. names.fs_type is required and has no default: 0 (installable) here because the example is built from MIT parameters; use 4 (Preview & Print) for a proprietary face, 0 for an open one; 2 (Restricted) makes some tools refuse the font; browsers ignore the field for web fonts. typo_metrics is an optional override and is left out here: hhea and OS/2 typo then both carry the measured glyph extent with a line gap of 0.",
